## Where an old chapter goes

You have rewritten a chapter and you want the old one where you can still read it.

Put it in another binder.

## Making the copy

- Select the chapter in the *Binder* panel. Press `Ctrl+D`, or choose *Document ▸
  Duplicate*. The copy keeps the same title and lands after the original and everything
  under it.
- Select the copy, the second of the two. Duplicating leaves your selection on the
  original, so rename the copy only once you have picked it, with *Document ▸ Rename*.
- A project started from a novel template already has a *Notes* binder. If yours has none,
  the button at the top of the *Binder* panel holds *New binder…*.
- Drag the copy onto that binder. If the button names a single binder rather than *All
  Binders*, choose *Show all binders* first, so both ends of the drag show.

That is all. If the rewrite turns out to be the worse of the two, drag it back.

## Why another binder is enough

A book runs from its own marker to the next one, inside the binder it lives in. See
[how a book is put together](:help-writing-model).

So an old chapter in another binder is outside the book. The word count, your targets and
pace, and the export leave it out.

## What still works on it

Everything about reading and editing. The old chapter keeps its title and its place in the
binder you chose. It is still found by search, still spellchecked, still backed up.

Your story bible still works there. If a character is named in the old draft, her entry
still counts those scenes.

## The other ways, and when they fit

- *Trash* is for something you have decided against. A trashed item leaves the *Binder*
  panel and stops counting, and stays recoverable. You can still open one from the *Trash*
  panel to read it, but it is filed as discarded, not kept.
- The *Versions* panel keeps what one piece of text said before, and can put an older state
  back. Reach for it to answer "what did this paragraph say yesterday". It works one item
  at a time, and restoring replaces what is there now. See
  [backups and versions](:help-backups-and-versions).
- *Include in exports*, in the Inspector, decides whether an item reaches the finished
  book. Switch it off and the item is left out when you export the book, and out of your
  word counts.
